/Title (Following the financial crisis of 2008-2013, real estate prices in Spain began to increase steadily, and the pandemic has provided a significant boost to that trend. Since 2021, we have observed a sustained rise in demand, with the entire market continuing to experience robust growth, achieving double-digit increases year after year!  Whether this will endure is uncertain, but the rationale behind our conviction that this trend will persist is as follows: increasing interest from diverse international assets \(United States, Poland, Canada, China, etc.\))
/Dest [13 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 1368 0 R
/Next 1480 0 R
>>
endobj
1464 0 obj
<<
/Title (In recent years, numerous new projects launched by developers have re-entered the market. It is essential to engage the services of an objective real estate agent who possesses a comprehensive understanding of the local market to guide you in identifying the most promising investment opportunities among these projects. Consulting the developer directly may lead to a biased perspective, as they are likely to promote their own project as "the best." A real estate agent in Spain can provide access to all projects along the Costa del Sol, ensuring an impartial viewpoint. Experts assert that real estate will continue to be an appealing asset and a secure investment for all buyers.)
